--- Test/dev infrastructure — NOT distributed with this package ---

MinIO / coollabsio/minio RELEASE.2025-10-15T17-29-55Z
  (digest sha256:69b55a1c1c5dc285ce04db96689f5b2102317fc77a50680a1874ca6efd1c87f9;
  a third-party build of the final upstream release tag)
  / AGPL-3.0 / https://github.com/minio/minio
  External S3-compatible SERVICE CONTAINER used ONLY by this package's own
  test suite (packages/ne-storage/tests/test_s3_conformance.py,
  test_s3_worm_live.py) and the optional `worm` dev-compose profile
  (deploy/compose/dev/compose.yaml) to obtain a real Object
  Lock/COMPLIANCE-mode-capable S3 endpoint to test against. NOT embedded, NOT
  distributed with this package, and NEVER part of a shipped deployment
  profile — production deployments configure NE_STORAGE_S3_* to point at the
  customer's own S3 / S3-compatible WORM storage. This is the LAST image
  MinIO published to Docker Hub before publishing stopped (Oct 2025); the
  upstream community repository went maintenance-mode (Dec 2025) and was
  archived (2026-04-25) — pinned by exact digest since no newer tag will ever
  appear. Chosen over SeaweedFS (this repo's existing dev-compose S3 gateway,
  used by the `langfuse` profile) specifically because SeaweedFS's Object
  Lock does not enforce COMPLIANCE-mode retention
  (seaweedfs/seaweedfs#8350, #7194) — using it for the WORM test lane would
  make the proof vacuous.

There is deliberately NO Azure equivalent of the MinIO test container:
Azurite (the Azure Storage emulator) does NOT implement immutability
policies, so it cannot prove the Azure WORM guarantee and is not used. The
azure_blob adapter's server-side proof is LIVE-PARKED against a real storage
account (packages/ne-storage/tests/test_azure_blob_worm_live.py, the
owner-gated NE-WORM-LIVE lane).

No third-party code is embedded in this package beyond the Python
dependencies listed above (all Apache-2.0/MIT/BSD-2-Clause/BSD-3-Clause,
C4-clean at the pinned versions). MinIO is consumed at test/dev time only, as
an external out-of-process service container.
